message.content:
Critically review two paper analyses in project `2026-11-12-llm-based-vs-traditional-static-analysis` (workspace /Users/makky/Downloads/AI-Research-Lab-main; project dir research/2026-11-12-llm-based-vs-traditional-static-analysis/).

Keys: `tashenova2026real` (WordPress PHP CVE benchmark, BDCC 2026, MDPI) and `deininger2026open` ("Open or Frontier?", Computers 2026, MDPI). Both peer-reviewed, full text in papers/<key>/fulltext.txt.

For each, check papers/<key>/analysis.md against fulltext.txt:
- every number and quote is supported at the cited page;
- [V]/[A]/[I] labels are correct;
- evidence strengths are justified;
- limitations, validity threats and COI are appraised fairly;
- relevance to RQ1–RQ5 (RESEARCH-QUESTIONS.md) holds.
Rules: docs/research-standards.md.

Specific points to verify:
- tashenova2026real: the analyst's own trivial-baseline arithmetic. It derives 74.5% / 46.2% prevalence from Table 2 and always-vulnerable macro-F1 ≈ 0.316 (Variant B). Check it against the counts. Also check that the "SAST misses ~98%" result is clearly scoped to an unnamed bespoke lexical taint analyser.
- deininger2026open: the always-flag F1 ≈ 0.043 at 1:44 and the derived F1 values for best LLM / Flawfinder / CodeBERT at 1:44. The cost and energy per true positive (Table 5, p. 8). The analyst flags internal inconsistencies in the paper: Gemma measured vs estimated energy; reasoning multiplier 2.5–7.6× vs 4.5–12.1×; "balanced by construction" vs 35.4% positive. Confirm these are real and handled correctly. Also check the "Claude Opus 5/Sonnet 5 writing assistance" disclosure (p. 27).

Do NOT write files (the harness blocks subagent Write). Return findings as text: per paper a verdict (pass / fix-needed) and a numbered list of findings, each with location in analysis.md, the problem, the evidence (fulltext page) and the exact suggested fix. Finish with cross-paper observations relevant to the evidence matrix (contradictions/agreements with other project papers, e.g. ding2025vulnerability, tan2026think, lu2025lab on PrimeVul/realistic prevalence).

